# Strumming: Waltz (Bass-Strum-Strum) (repertoire plan: st-strum-waltz). Your part: D (xx0232)
# for 2 bars, A7 (x02020) for 2, four times: 16 bars of 3/4. Beat 1 is the bass note alone, the
# open string 4 (D) under D and the open string 5 (A) under A7; beats 2 and 3 are light
# downstrums on strings 3 to 1 only. The strums are written out as the three notes they sound
# (D: A D F#; A7: G C# E, with the open string 3), so the tab shows exactly which strings to hit.
# Hold the whole chord shape all the time: the bass is open, but the fingers are already down.
# The teacher plays an original waltz tune in D whose note on beat 1 belongs to the chord in force.
# It ends on A over A7, a half close that leads straight back to bar 1 when you loop the study.
title: Strumming: Waltz (Bass-Strum-Strum)
